WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:03.509
Optimization philosophy is something

2
00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:07.030
we want to cover because optimization isn't something

3
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.830
that should be done at one stage or another stage

4
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.269
of your project, but something that

5
00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:15.310
should be done at every stage.

6
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.109
Whenever your project is starting,

7
00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:18.809
whenever your project is in the middle,

8
00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:21.489
and even until the end of your project,

9
00:00:21.489 --> 00:00:26.280
optimization is an ongoing effort.

10
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.760
Optimizing your Unreal Engine 5 project

11
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.899
is also going to be the result of many small optimizations.

12
00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:37.179
There will be no one single optimization

13
00:00:37.179 --> 00:00:41.500
that will help any poorly performing project run better.

14
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.500
Because of this, you need to ensure

15
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.600
that you're checking your project's optimization using

16
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.880
the techniques in this tutorial series

17
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.100
at every stage of your project.

18
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.679
This will ensure that if there are any performance issues,

19
00:00:56.679 --> 00:00:59.520
they can quickly be addressed and rectified

20
00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.579
and your project will ship on time with the features

21
00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:07.180
you intended to use and look exactly like you want it.
